  "notes": [
    "Compound of *poner* — follows the same irregular patterns throughout.",
    "Irregular yo present: *dispongo* (go-verb), same pattern as *poner→pongo*.",
    "Irregular preterite stem: *dispus-* (dispuse, dispusiste, dispuso...).",
    "Irregular future/conditional stem: *dispondr-* (dispondré, dispondría).",
    "Subjuntivo built from the yo stem: *dispong-* (disponga, dispongas...).",
    "Irregular past participle, inherited from *poner→puesto*: **dispuesto**.",
    "Imperativo tú affirmative is irregular, following *poner→pon*: **dispón**.",
    "Often used with \"de\": *disponer de algo* (\"to have something available/at one's disposal\").",
    "*Dispone de una historia real conmovedora.* (\"He has a moving true story at his disposal.\")",
    "*No disponemos de mucho tiempo.* (\"We don't have much time available.\")",
    "Related: *la disposición* (arrangement/disposal, noun), *disponible* (available, adjective), *disponerse a* (reflexive, \"to get ready to\")."
  ],
